00:17:07.872 --> 00:17:09.393
- Let me first unmute myself.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.203
Good morning, Yale College Class of 2021.

00:17:15.203 --> 00:17:18.036
(people cheering)

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:29.530
Welcome to the graduates of
Grace Hopper, Jonathan Edwards,

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:34.530
Trumbull, Silliman,
and Ezra Stiles College

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:40.710
who have arrived on Old
Campus to begin our ceremony,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:44.460
and welcome to family, friends
and members of the class

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:48.210
who are joining us virtually
today via livestream.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:52.120
We are so excited to have
arrived on this special day.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.983
In a few moments we will
begin announcing the graduates

00:17:54.983 --> 00:17:58.510
as they process across
the commencement stage

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.543
here in front of me.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.880
Before we start our program,
a few words about the land

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:07.020
on which today's ceremony is taking place.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.990
Yale acknowledges that
indigenous peoples and nations

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:14.676
including Mohegan, Mashantucket
Pequot, Eastern Pequot,

00:18:14.676 --> 00:18:18.870
Schaghticoke, Golden
Hill Paugussett, Niantic,

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.620
and the Quinnipiac and other
Algonquin-speaking peoples

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:26.090
have stewarded through generations
the lands and waterways

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:28.600
of what is now the state of Connecticut.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:32.450
We honor and respect the
enduring relationship that exists

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:36.200
between these peoples and
nations and this land.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.263
Thank you and please enjoy the program.

00:18:42.111 --> 00:18:44.944
(people clapping)

