00:51:03.857 --> 00:51:07.650
- To the students of the Class of 2021

00:51:07.650 --> 00:51:10.010
and their parents, families and friends

00:51:10.010 --> 00:51:12.253
looking on from around the globe,

00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:16.810
we gather to recognize the
extraordinary accomplishments

00:51:16.810 --> 00:51:20.050
of all of you who have worked so hard

00:51:20.050 --> 00:51:22.683
to complete your programs of study.

00:51:23.740 --> 00:51:27.540
We salute your efforts, your diligence,

00:51:27.540 --> 00:51:30.373
your talent and your intellect.

00:51:31.250 --> 00:51:34.370
We also join you in expressing gratitude

00:51:34.370 --> 00:51:38.350
for all who have supported
you in these endeavors.

00:51:38.350 --> 00:51:42.170
Your families and friends, teachers

00:51:42.170 --> 00:51:44.293
and other members of the Yale community.

00:51:45.180 --> 00:51:48.200
Congratulations Class of 2021.

00:51:49.955 --> 00:51:52.788
(people cheering)

00:52:18.490 --> 00:52:20.810
- Hello, Class of 2021.

00:52:20.810 --> 00:52:23.740
My name is Steven
Orientale and I am a member

00:52:23.740 --> 00:52:27.440
of the Class Day committee
and the Senior Class Council.

00:52:27.440 --> 00:52:30.640
Four years have gone by
in the blink of an eye.

00:52:30.640 --> 00:52:33.210
We've made so many memories
from the first year

00:52:33.210 --> 00:52:35.870
snowball fight on Old Campus right here,

00:52:35.870 --> 00:52:38.610
to the Yale-Harvard football game of 2019,

00:52:38.610 --> 00:52:41.000
where we won in double overtime,

00:52:41.000 --> 00:52:44.060
to all the late nights,
whether they be in a library

00:52:44.060 --> 00:52:46.780
studying for an exam,
or in the common room

00:52:46.780 --> 00:52:49.400
talking with our friends and teammates.

00:52:49.400 --> 00:52:51.910
Although our senior year
experience was certainly

00:52:51.910 --> 00:52:55.220
not a traditional one, the Class of 2021

00:52:55.220 --> 00:52:57.300
made the best of the situation.

00:52:57.300 --> 00:53:00.560
When we leave Yale in just
a few days, we will leave

00:53:00.560 --> 00:53:03.370
with memories and friendships
that will last a lifetime.

00:53:03.370 --> 00:53:06.768
Here's the class of 2021. We did it.

00:53:06.768 --> 00:53:09.601
(people cheering)

00:53:23.310 --> 00:53:25.410
- Class of 2021, good morning.

00:53:25.410 --> 00:53:26.780
My name is Stanley Lam.

00:53:26.780 --> 00:53:28.130
- And I'm Jin Li.

00:53:28.130 --> 00:53:29.790
- And we are members of the committee

00:53:29.790 --> 00:53:31.840
that organized Class Day, which will air

00:53:31.840 --> 00:53:34.440
on YouTube tomorrow at 2:30 PM.

00:53:34.440 --> 00:53:37.580
- Two minutes before 2:30 at 2:28 PM,

00:53:37.580 --> 00:53:39.920
a special piece written
by our Class Day speaker

00:53:39.920 --> 00:53:42.150
Robert Lopez will be
played from Harkness Tower,

00:53:42.150 --> 00:53:44.060
so keep your ears open.

00:53:44.060 --> 00:53:46.130
- If you haven't already
decorated a funny hat

00:53:46.130 --> 00:53:48.300
for Class Day, it's not too late.

00:53:48.300 --> 00:53:50.350
- In fact, on your seat
today, you received

00:53:50.350 --> 00:53:53.020
a Class Day 2021 hat that
you might want to use

00:53:53.020 --> 00:53:54.500
just for that purpose.

00:53:54.500 --> 00:53:57.140
- You'll also find a gift
bag, which includes items

00:53:57.140 --> 00:53:59.660
that represent long-standing
Class Day traditions,

00:53:59.660 --> 00:54:01.010
as well as others that are new

00:54:01.010 --> 00:54:03.200
and unique to the Class of 2021.

00:54:03.200 --> 00:54:04.860
- In addition to the Class Day speaker,

00:54:04.860 --> 00:54:06.920
tomorrow's program also includes remarks

00:54:06.920 --> 00:54:09.130
by members of our class
who have put together

00:54:09.130 --> 00:54:11.520
outstanding original speeches.

00:54:11.520 --> 00:54:13.980
- And because Class
Day is about all of us,

00:54:13.980 --> 00:54:16.040
you'll see your photographs
and video reflections

00:54:16.040 --> 00:54:17.690
throughout tomorrow's program.

00:54:17.690 --> 00:54:21.896
- Congratulations class of
2021, and see you at Class Day,

00:54:21.896 --> 00:54:24.729
(people cheering)

00:54:42.350 --> 00:54:45.980
- Class of 2021, congratulations again.

00:54:45.980 --> 00:54:48.520
I am so happy to be with you

00:54:48.520 --> 00:54:50.750
and to celebrate with you today.

00:54:50.750 --> 00:54:53.450
Graduating is a great accomplishment,

00:54:53.450 --> 00:54:56.050
one of the most important
ones of your life,

00:54:56.050 --> 00:54:59.970
and if you think back to when
you first arrived on campus,

00:54:59.970 --> 00:55:02.000
no one could have imagined
that you would live through

00:55:02.000 --> 00:55:05.630
a global pandemic before
reaching this moment,

00:55:05.630 --> 00:55:09.810
but you did, and thanks to
your strength and perseverance,

00:55:09.810 --> 00:55:12.330
this moment has finally come.

00:55:12.330 --> 00:55:15.120
I'm honored to recognize all
the work that you have done

00:55:15.120 --> 00:55:18.540
to get here, much of it with
the support of your family

00:55:18.540 --> 00:55:22.363
and friends, so today is your
day and it is theirs too.

00:55:23.310 --> 00:55:26.180
Today is a day for looking back with pride

00:55:26.180 --> 00:55:27.870
at everything you have accomplished

00:55:27.870 --> 00:55:30.120
and all the goals you have reached.

00:55:30.120 --> 00:55:32.530
Of course, it brings some sadness too,

00:55:32.530 --> 00:55:35.930
now that you are ending
your bright college years.

00:55:35.930 --> 00:55:38.020
But today is a commencement, a beginning,

00:55:38.020 --> 00:55:41.180
so now as you look to
the days and years ahead,

00:55:41.180 --> 00:55:43.920
think of the new achievements
and opportunities

00:55:43.920 --> 00:55:47.079
in front of you and look around as well,

00:55:47.079 --> 00:55:50.264
to remind yourself of
the excellent company

00:55:50.264 --> 00:55:52.680
joining you on the new beginning,

00:55:52.680 --> 00:55:54.623
your friendships formed at Yale.

00:55:55.920 --> 00:55:58.330
Tomorrow you will celebrate
Class Day, a tradition

00:55:58.330 --> 00:56:02.070
stretching back 150 years
in Yale College history.

00:56:02.070 --> 00:56:05.890
I'm excited to watch the
virtual program along with you,

00:56:05.890 --> 00:56:07.930
and on Monday, we can look forward

00:56:07.930 --> 00:56:11.260
to President Salovey's
commencement address.

00:56:11.260 --> 00:56:13.210
I'm grateful to the Class Day committee,

00:56:13.210 --> 00:56:15.990
to the Senior Class
Council, to the University

00:56:15.990 --> 00:56:19.230
secretary's office, to your
college heads and deans,

00:56:19.230 --> 00:56:21.460
and to everyone who contributed to making

00:56:21.460 --> 00:56:24.970
the special events of
this weekend possible.

00:56:24.970 --> 00:56:27.530
And I'm most appreciative to you,

00:56:27.530 --> 00:56:29.540
for all that you have brought to Yale

00:56:29.540 --> 00:56:32.350
and will now bring out
into the world with you.

00:56:32.350 --> 00:56:35.809
Again, Class of 2021, congratulations.

00:56:35.809 --> 00:56:38.642
(people cheering)

00:56:48.274 --> 00:56:51.107
(classical music)

01:04:02.204 --> 01:04:04.787
(upbeat music)

